From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:09:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 154/185] The timeshare read works: Doom's loop, mirrored, both
 carry tests were inverted

With the interlock keeping the servant off, the firmware's read finally
ran far enough to show its own bugs. Two, both against Doom's sub
program at $6898, and both now fixed by mirroring it instruction for
instruction:

The destination. $4146's job -- select sub-CPU host read before
CDCREAD -- was missing entirely, and the first fix (a byte store of 3)
was wrong in a subtler way: the byte at $FF8004 also carries EDT and
DSR, and overwriting them cut every transfer to a 32-byte fragment.
Doom does a read-modify-write: andi.w #$F8FF then ori.w #$0300.

The carry sense, on both calls that move data. Doom retries CDCREAD
while carry is SET and proceeds on clear; ours retried while carry was
CLEAR -- re-arming the byte counter after every successful arm. Doom
treats a carry-SET CDCTRN as failed and goes back to CDCSTAT; ours
treated it as finished and ACKed. Every sector the old loop "delivered"
was accounting, not data: rc 0, counters perfect, scratch full of
zeros. "The folder opened and listed no files" end to end.

Proof, headless: CDTEST now auto-runs under the emulator (Down held via
the input script, log recovered from cart SRAM through a core patch),
and twelve consecutive rounds mount D:, list READCD.TXT and read its
contents -- every firmware round clean, rd counting real deliveries.

Known and kept in view: the fallback rounds (ts off, our own CDC
driver) mostly pass but show wrong-sector churn in the emulator (why
5555 on two rounds of twelve). The shipping path serves D: through the
firmware, so this is a fallback-quality issue, logged, not blocking.

Also: holding Down at power-on now runs CDTEST from autoexec -- on
hardware it saves the desktop navigation, in the harness it is what
makes headless diagnostics possible at all.
---
 bios/bios.c    | 12 ++++++++++++
 bios/scdapi.h  |  2 +-
 bios/segacd2.S | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/bios.c b/bios/bios.c
index ccd8d23..c259e7f 100644
--- a/bios/bios.c
+++ b/bios/bios.c
@@ -744,6 +744,18 @@ static void autoexec(void)
     DTA dta;
     WORD err;
 
+#ifdef MACHINE_SEGACD
+    /* Down held at power-on: run the disc diagnostic without a person
+     * navigating the desktop. On hardware that saves d-pad gymnastics;
+     * in the emulator harness it is the difference between having a
+     * diagnostic and not, because the harness cannot drive the mouse
+     * to CDTEST's icon -- and CDLOG.TXT lands in cart SRAM, which the
+     * harness persists as cart.brm, so a full eight-round hardware-
+     * shaped log can now come out of a headless emulator run. */
+    if (segacd_diag)
+        Pexec(PE_LOADGO, "A:\\CDTEST.PRG", "", NULL);
+#endif
+
     /* check if the user does not want to run AUTO programs */
     if (bootflags & BOOTFLAG_SKIP_AUTO_ACC)
         return;
diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index a673879..9564150 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  22
+#define SCD_VERSION  23
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
diff --git a/bios/segacd2.S b/bios/segacd2.S
index 2d8fec9..9654a7e 100644
--- a/bios/segacd2.S
+++ b/bios/segacd2.S
@@ -695,19 +695,42 @@ brd_stat:
         move.w  d0,50(a5)
         jsr     0x5F22
         bcs     brd_stat                // no sector ready yet
+
+        // Doom's loop, mirrored instruction for instruction from its
+        // sub program at $6898 -- because ours had the carry tests
+        // INVERTED on both calls that move data, and the destination
+        // write wrong besides. What Doom does between CDCSTAT and
+        // CDCREAD:
+        //
+        //   68a2: andi.w #$F8FF,$FF8004    clear the destination bits
+        //   68a8: ori.w  #$0300,$FF8004    sub-CPU host read
+        //   68ae: CDCREAD;  bcs 68ae       retry while carry SET
+        //   68c0: CDCTRN;   bcs 6886       carry SET = failed, re-STAT
+        //   68ce: CDCACK
+        //
+        // A read-modify-write, not a byte store: the byte at $FF8004
+        // also carries EDT and DSR, and overwriting them is what cut
+        // the last attempt's transfers to 32-byte fragments. And the
+        // carry sense: ours retried CDCREAD while carry was CLEAR --
+        // that is, re-armed the byte counter after every successful
+        // arm -- and treated a failed CDCTRN as a finished one. Every
+        // sector "delivered" by the previous shape of this loop was
+        // accounting, not data.
+        andi.w  #0xF8FF,0xFF8004
+        ori.w   #0x0300,0xFF8004
 brd_read:
         cmpi.l  #200,_segacd_bios_frames
         bcc     brd_fail_read
         move.w  #0x008B,d0              // CDCREAD
         move.w  d0,50(a5)
         jsr     0x5F22
-        bcc     brd_read
+        bcs     brd_read                // not accepted yet: re-ask
         movea.l 8(a5),a0                // where this sector goes
         lea     12(a5),a1               // header scratch
         move.w  #0x008C,d0              // CDCTRN
         move.w  d0,50(a5)
         jsr     0x5F22
-        bcc     brd_read                // transfer incomplete, go again
+        bcs     brd_stat                // failed: wait for another sector
         move.w  #0x008D,d0              // CDCACK
         move.w  d0,50(a5)
         jsr     0x5F22
